;/* share & organise 2026-08-17 */(function(H){for(var l in H){window.PS_I18N[l]=Object.assign(window.PS_I18N[l]||{},H[l]);}})({"es":{"Build it together.":"Constrúyanlo juntos.","Or just send them a copy.":"O simplemente envía una copia.","The best question you ever wrote shouldn't die in your own account. Invite someone to edit a poll, survey, quiz or study set alongside you — or send them a copy to make their own. Either way it works by email, with anyone: on your team or not, on any plan, signed up or not.":"La mejor pregunta que has escrito no debería morir en tu propia cuenta. Invita a alguien a editar contigo una encuesta, sondeo, cuestionario o set de estudio — o envíale una copia para que la haga suya. En ambos casos funciona por correo, con quien sea: de tu equipo o no, con cualquier plan, registrado o no.","Build it together":"Constrúyanlo juntos","Two people, one deck, live.":"Dos personas, un proyecto, en vivo.","You both edit the same quiz and see each other's changes as they happen. You'll know who's in the deck and which question they're on, so you never write over each other. You stay the owner and can end it at any time — instantly, even mid-edit.":"Los dos editáis el mismo cuestionario y veis los cambios del otro según ocurren. Sabrás quién está en el proyecto y en qué pregunta, así que nunca os pisáis. Tú sigues siendo el propietario y puedes terminarlo cuando quieras — al instante, incluso a mitad de edición.","Or send a copy":"O envía una copia","Their version, their rules.":"Su versión, sus reglas.","When it's a hand-off rather than a collaboration, send a copy instead. It lands in their library as their own deck — they can rewrite every question and run it with their class, and nothing they do touches your original.":"Cuando es una entrega y no una colaboración, envía una copia. Aparece en su biblioteca como proyecto propio — pueden reescribir cada pregunta y usarlo con su clase, y nada de lo que hagan afecta a tu original.","Folders that fit a term":"Carpetas que encajan con el curso","One lesson, all its material, together.":"Una clase, todo su material, junto.","Group by class, unit or event — and a folder holds any mix of products. Your warm-up poll, your graded quiz and your revision set finally sit side by side instead of in four separate tabs.":"Agrupa por clase, unidad o evento — y una carpeta admite cualquier mezcla de productos. Tu encuesta de calentamiento, tu cuestionario calificado y tu set de repaso por fin están uno al lado del otro en vez de en cuatro pestañas distintas.","No workspace to join, no seat to buy":"Sin espacio al que unirse, sin asiento que comprar","Collaboration shouldn't require sharing a bill.":"Colaborar no debería exigir compartir una factura.","Most tools make you add someone to a workspace before you can work with them — which means the same organisation, often the same subscription. PollSlide shares one deck at a time. Two teachers at different schools on separate personal plans can build a quiz together this afternoon, and nobody sees anything else in the other's account.":"La mayoría de herramientas te obligan a añadir a alguien a un espacio de trabajo antes de poder trabajar con esa persona — lo que implica la misma organización y, a menudo, la misma suscripción. PollSlide comparte un proyecto cada vez. Dos profesores de escuelas distintas con planes personales separados pueden crear un cuestionario juntos esta misma tarde, y ninguno ve nada más de la cuenta del otro.","Live collaboration":"Colaboración en vivo","Build a quiz with someone in real time — even if they're not on your team or your plan. See who's editing what; you stay the owner and can end it any time.":"Crea un cuestionario con alguien en tiempo real — aunque no esté en tu equipo ni en tu plan. Mira quién edita qué; tú sigues siendo el propietario y puedes terminarlo cuando quieras.","Share with anyone":"Comparte con quien quieras","Send any deck to a colleague by email — on your team or not. They get their own copy to edit; yours never changes.":"Envía cualquier proyecto a un colega por correo — de tu equipo o no. Recibe su propia copia para editar; la tuya nunca cambia.","Folders & search":"Carpetas y búsqueda","Group a whole lesson together whatever its type, pin what you run weekly, and search inside your questions — not just their titles.":"Agrupa una clase entera sea cual sea su tipo, fija lo que usas cada semana y busca dentro de tus preguntas — no solo en sus títulos.","Find it in a keystroke — even at two hundred decks":"Encuéntralo con una tecla — incluso con doscientos proyectos","Search reads your questions, not just your titles.":"La búsqueda lee tus preguntas, no solo tus títulos.","Type “Punnett” and it finds the quiz wherever you filed it, then tells you where that is. Pin the handful you run every week to the top. Sort by what you actually opened last. Archive last term without deleting a thing. Built for the teacher on their third year of material, not the demo account with four.":"Escribe «Punnett» y encuentra el cuestionario dondequiera que lo hayas archivado, y te dice dónde está. Fija arriba los pocos que usas cada semana. Ordena por lo que abriste de verdad. Archiva el curso pasado sin borrar nada. Hecho para el profesor en su tercer año de material, no para la cuenta de demostración con cuatro.","Can two of us build the same quiz at the same time?":"¿Podemos dos personas crear el mismo cuestionario a la vez?","Yes. Invite someone to edit and you both work on the same deck, seeing each other's changes as they happen. A question someone is typing into is marked so you can't write over them. You stay the owner throughout, and ending their access takes effect immediately — there's no session to wait out.":"Sí. Invita a alguien a editar y ambos trabajáis sobre el mismo proyecto, viendo los cambios del otro según ocurren. Una pregunta que alguien está escribiendo aparece marcada para que no la pises. Tú sigues siendo el propietario en todo momento, y quitar el acceso surte efecto de inmediato — no hay ninguna sesión que esperar.","Do we need to be in the same workspace or on the same plan?":"¿Tenemos que estar en el mismo espacio de trabajo o en el mismo plan?","No. That's the point. Collaboration is per-deck, not per-workspace — two people on separate personal plans, at different organisations, can build one quiz together. Your collaborator sees that deck and nothing else in your account.":"No. De eso se trata. La colaboración es por proyecto, no por espacio de trabajo — dos personas con planes personales distintos, en organizaciones distintas, pueden crear un cuestionario juntas. Tu colaborador ve ese proyecto y nada más de tu cuenta.","Can I share a quiz with a colleague who isn't on my team?":"¿Puedo compartir un cuestionario con un colega que no está en mi equipo?","Yes. Share any poll, survey, quiz or study set with any email address — no shared workspace, no matching plan, and they don't even need a PollSlide account yet. If they're new, the share is waiting the first time they sign in.":"Sí. Comparte cualquier encuesta, sondeo, cuestionario o set de estudio con cualquier dirección de correo — sin espacio compartido, sin necesidad del mismo plan, y ni siquiera necesitan tener cuenta de PollSlide. Si son nuevos, les espera la primera vez que inicien sesión.","If someone edits a deck I shared, does mine change too?":"Si alguien edita un proyecto que compartí, ¿cambia también el mío?","No. Accepting a share creates their own independent copy. They can rewrite every question and run it with their own class; your original is untouched. Equally, edits you make afterwards don't reach a copy you already sent.":"No. Al aceptar se crea su propia copia independiente. Pueden reescribir cada pregunta y usarla con su clase; tu original queda intacto. Del mismo modo, los cambios que hagas después no llegan a una copia ya enviada.","I teach several classes. Can I keep hundreds of decks organised?":"Doy varias clases. ¿Puedo mantener organizados cientos de proyectos?","Folders group by class, unit or event, and one folder holds any mix of products — so a lesson's warm-up poll, graded quiz and revision set sit together instead of in four separate tabs. Search looks inside your questions, not just their titles, and finds them wherever they're filed. Pin the ones you run weekly, and archive last term without deleting anything.":"Las carpetas agrupan por clase, unidad o evento, y una carpeta admite cualquier mezcla de productos — así la encuesta de calentamiento, el cuestionario calificado y el set de repaso de una clase están juntos en vez de en cuatro pestañas. La búsqueda mira dentro de tus preguntas, no solo en sus títulos, y las encuentra estén donde estén. Fija las que usas cada semana y archiva el curso pasado sin borrar nada.","Share & organise":"Comparte y organiza","Share":"Compartir"},"de":{"Build it together.":"Baut es gemeinsam.","Or just send them a copy.":"Oder schick einfach eine Kopie.","The best question you ever wrote shouldn't die in your own account. Invite someone to edit a poll, survey, quiz or study set alongside you — or send them a copy to make their own. Either way it works by email, with anyone: on your team or not, on any plan, signed up or not.":"Die beste Frage, die du je geschrieben hast, sollte nicht in deinem eigenen Konto versauern. Lade jemanden ein, eine Umfrage, ein Quiz oder ein Lernset gemeinsam mit dir zu bearbeiten — oder schick eine Kopie, die ganz ihm gehört. Beides läuft per E-Mail, mit wem du willst: im Team oder nicht, in jedem Tarif, registriert oder nicht.","Build it together":"Gemeinsam bauen","Two people, one deck, live.":"Zwei Personen, ein Projekt, live.","You both edit the same quiz and see each other's changes as they happen. You'll know who's in the deck and which question they're on, so you never write over each other. You stay the owner and can end it at any time — instantly, even mid-edit.":"Ihr bearbeitet dasselbe Quiz und seht die Änderungen des anderen, während sie passieren. Du siehst, wer im Projekt ist und an welcher Frage — so überschreibt ihr euch nie. Du bleibst Eigentümer und kannst es jederzeit beenden — sofort, auch mitten im Bearbeiten.","Or send a copy":"Oder eine Kopie schicken","Their version, their rules.":"Ihre Version, ihre Regeln.","When it's a hand-off rather than a collaboration, send a copy instead. It lands in their library as their own deck — they can rewrite every question and run it with their class, and nothing they do touches your original.":"Wenn es eine Übergabe ist und keine Zusammenarbeit, schick stattdessen eine Kopie. Sie landet als eigenes Projekt in ihrer Bibliothek — sie können jede Frage umschreiben und es in ihrer Klasse nutzen, und nichts davon berührt dein Original.","Folders that fit a term":"Ordner, die zum Semester passen","One lesson, all its material, together.":"Eine Stunde, ihr ganzes Material, beisammen.","Group by class, unit or event — and a folder holds any mix of products. Your warm-up poll, your graded quiz and your revision set finally sit side by side instead of in four separate tabs.":"Gruppiere nach Klasse, Einheit oder Veranstaltung — und ein Ordner fasst jede Mischung an Produkten. Deine Aufwärm-Umfrage, dein benotetes Quiz und dein Lernset liegen endlich nebeneinander statt in vier getrennten Tabs.","No workspace to join, no seat to buy":"Kein Workspace zum Beitreten, kein Platz zum Kaufen","Collaboration shouldn't require sharing a bill.":"Zusammenarbeit sollte keine gemeinsame Rechnung voraussetzen.","Most tools make you add someone to a workspace before you can work with them — which means the same organisation, often the same subscription. PollSlide shares one deck at a time. Two teachers at different schools on separate personal plans can build a quiz together this afternoon, and nobody sees anything else in the other's account.":"Die meisten Tools verlangen, jemanden erst in einen Workspace aufzunehmen — also dieselbe Organisation und oft dasselbe Abo. PollSlide teilt immer nur ein Projekt. Zwei Lehrkräfte an verschiedenen Schulen mit getrennten privaten Tarifen können heute Nachmittag gemeinsam ein Quiz bauen, und keiner sieht sonst etwas im Konto des anderen.","Live collaboration":"Live-Zusammenarbeit","Build a quiz with someone in real time — even if they're not on your team or your plan. See who's editing what; you stay the owner and can end it any time.":"Baue ein Quiz mit jemandem in Echtzeit — auch wenn er nicht in deinem Team oder Tarif ist. Sieh, wer was bearbeitet; du bleibst Eigentümer und kannst es jederzeit beenden.","Share with anyone":"Mit allen teilen","Send any deck to a colleague by email — on your team or not. They get their own copy to edit; yours never changes.":"Schick jedes Projekt per E-Mail an eine Kollegin — im Team oder nicht. Sie bekommt ihre eigene Kopie zum Bearbeiten; deine ändert sich nie.","Folders & search":"Ordner & Suche","Group a whole lesson together whatever its type, pin what you run weekly, and search inside your questions — not just their titles.":"Fasse eine ganze Stunde zusammen, egal welcher Typ, hefte an, was du wöchentlich nutzt, und suche in deinen Fragen — nicht nur in den Titeln.","Find it in a keystroke — even at two hundred decks":"Mit einem Tastendruck gefunden — auch bei zweihundert Projekten","Search reads your questions, not just your titles.":"Die Suche liest deine Fragen, nicht nur die Titel.","Type “Punnett” and it finds the quiz wherever you filed it, then tells you where that is. Pin the handful you run every week to the top. Sort by what you actually opened last. Archive last term without deleting a thing. Built for the teacher on their third year of material, not the demo account with four.":"Tippe „Punnett“ und es findet das Quiz, egal wo du es abgelegt hast — und sagt dir, wo das ist. Hefte die Handvoll an, die du jede Woche nutzt. Sortiere danach, was du zuletzt wirklich geöffnet hast. Archiviere das letzte Semester, ohne etwas zu löschen. Gebaut für die Lehrkraft im dritten Jahr, nicht für das Demokonto mit vier Einträgen.","Can two of us build the same quiz at the same time?":"Können wir zu zweit gleichzeitig am selben Quiz arbeiten?","Yes. Invite someone to edit and you both work on the same deck, seeing each other's changes as they happen. A question someone is typing into is marked so you can't write over them. You stay the owner throughout, and ending their access takes effect immediately — there's no session to wait out.":"Ja. Lade jemanden zum Bearbeiten ein, und ihr arbeitet beide am selben Projekt und seht die Änderungen des anderen live. Eine Frage, in die gerade jemand tippt, ist markiert, damit du sie nicht überschreibst. Du bleibst durchgehend Eigentümer, und der Entzug des Zugriffs wirkt sofort — es gibt keine Sitzung, die erst ablaufen müsste.","Do we need to be in the same workspace or on the same plan?":"Müssen wir im selben Workspace oder im selben Tarif sein?","No. That's the point. Collaboration is per-deck, not per-workspace — two people on separate personal plans, at different organisations, can build one quiz together. Your collaborator sees that deck and nothing else in your account.":"Nein. Genau darum geht es. Zusammenarbeit läuft pro Projekt, nicht pro Workspace — zwei Personen mit getrennten privaten Tarifen in verschiedenen Organisationen können gemeinsam ein Quiz bauen. Dein Mitarbeiter sieht dieses eine Projekt und sonst nichts in deinem Konto.","Can I share a quiz with a colleague who isn't on my team?":"Kann ich ein Quiz mit jemandem teilen, der nicht in meinem Team ist?","Yes. Share any poll, survey, quiz or study set with any email address — no shared workspace, no matching plan, and they don't even need a PollSlide account yet. If they're new, the share is waiting the first time they sign in.":"Ja. Teile jede Umfrage, jedes Quiz oder Lernset mit jeder E-Mail-Adresse — kein gemeinsamer Workspace, kein gleicher Tarif, und ein PollSlide-Konto braucht es noch nicht einmal. Sind sie neu, wartet die Freigabe beim ersten Login.","If someone edits a deck I shared, does mine change too?":"Wenn jemand ein geteiltes Projekt bearbeitet, ändert sich meins mit?","No. Accepting a share creates their own independent copy. They can rewrite every question and run it with their own class; your original is untouched. Equally, edits you make afterwards don't reach a copy you already sent.":"Nein. Beim Annehmen entsteht eine eigene, unabhängige Kopie. Sie können jede Frage umschreiben und es in ihrer Klasse nutzen; dein Original bleibt unberührt. Ebenso erreichen spätere Änderungen von dir eine bereits verschickte Kopie nicht mehr.","I teach several classes. Can I keep hundreds of decks organised?":"Ich unterrichte mehrere Klassen. Kann ich Hunderte Projekte organisiert halten?","Folders group by class, unit or event, and one folder holds any mix of products — so a lesson's warm-up poll, graded quiz and revision set sit together instead of in four separate tabs. Search looks inside your questions, not just their titles, and finds them wherever they're filed. Pin the ones you run weekly, and archive last term without deleting anything.":"Ordner gruppieren nach Klasse, Einheit oder Veranstaltung, und ein Ordner fasst jede Mischung an Produkten — so liegen Aufwärm-Umfrage, benotetes Quiz und Lernset einer Stunde beisammen statt in vier getrennten Tabs. Die Suche schaut in deine Fragen, nicht nur in die Titel, und findet sie, wo immer sie abgelegt sind. Hefte an, was du wöchentlich nutzt, und archiviere das letzte Semester, ohne etwas zu löschen.","Share & organise":"Teilen & organisieren","Share":"Teilen"},"fr":{"Build it together.":"Construisez-le ensemble.","Or just send them a copy.":"Ou envoyez-leur simplement une copie.","The best question you ever wrote shouldn't die in your own account. Invite someone to edit a poll, survey, quiz or study set alongside you — or send them a copy to make their own. Either way it works by email, with anyone: on your team or not, on any plan, signed up or not.":"La meilleure question que vous ayez écrite ne devrait pas mourir dans votre propre compte. Invitez quelqu'un à modifier un sondage, un questionnaire, un quiz ou un set de révision avec vous — ou envoyez-lui une copie qui devient la sienne. Dans les deux cas cela passe par e-mail, avec n'importe qui : de votre équipe ou non, quel que soit le forfait, inscrit ou non.","Build it together":"Construisez ensemble","Two people, one deck, live.":"Deux personnes, un projet, en direct.","You both edit the same quiz and see each other's changes as they happen. You'll know who's in the deck and which question they're on, so you never write over each other. You stay the owner and can end it at any time — instantly, even mid-edit.":"Vous modifiez tous les deux le même quiz et voyez les changements de l'autre au fur et à mesure. Vous savez qui est dans le projet et sur quelle question, donc vous ne vous écrasez jamais. Vous restez propriétaire et pouvez y mettre fin à tout moment — immédiatement, même en pleine modification.","Or send a copy":"Ou envoyez une copie","Their version, their rules.":"Sa version, ses règles.","When it's a hand-off rather than a collaboration, send a copy instead. It lands in their library as their own deck — they can rewrite every question and run it with their class, and nothing they do touches your original.":"Quand il s'agit d'une passation plutôt que d'une collaboration, envoyez plutôt une copie. Elle arrive dans sa bibliothèque comme son propre projet — il peut réécrire chaque question et l'utiliser avec sa classe, sans que rien ne touche votre original.","Folders that fit a term":"Des dossiers à l'échelle d'un trimestre","One lesson, all its material, together.":"Un cours, tout son matériel, au même endroit.","Group by class, unit or event — and a folder holds any mix of products. Your warm-up poll, your graded quiz and your revision set finally sit side by side instead of in four separate tabs.":"Regroupez par classe, unité ou événement — et un dossier accepte n'importe quel mélange de produits. Votre sondage d'échauffement, votre quiz noté et votre set de révision sont enfin côte à côte au lieu d'être dans quatre onglets séparés.","No workspace to join, no seat to buy":"Aucun espace à rejoindre, aucun siège à acheter","Collaboration shouldn't require sharing a bill.":"Collaborer ne devrait pas exiger de partager une facture.","Most tools make you add someone to a workspace before you can work with them — which means the same organisation, often the same subscription. PollSlide shares one deck at a time. Two teachers at different schools on separate personal plans can build a quiz together this afternoon, and nobody sees anything else in the other's account.":"La plupart des outils vous obligent à ajouter quelqu'un à un espace de travail avant de pouvoir travailler avec lui — donc la même organisation, souvent le même abonnement. PollSlide partage un projet à la fois. Deux enseignants d'établissements différents, sur des forfaits personnels distincts, peuvent construire un quiz ensemble cet après-midi, et aucun ne voit quoi que ce soit d'autre dans le compte de l'autre.","Live collaboration":"Collaboration en direct","Build a quiz with someone in real time — even if they're not on your team or your plan. See who's editing what; you stay the owner and can end it any time.":"Créez un quiz avec quelqu'un en temps réel — même s'il n'est ni dans votre équipe ni sur votre forfait. Voyez qui modifie quoi ; vous restez propriétaire et pouvez y mettre fin quand vous voulez.","Share with anyone":"Partagez avec qui vous voulez","Send any deck to a colleague by email — on your team or not. They get their own copy to edit; yours never changes.":"Envoyez n'importe quel projet à un collègue par e-mail — de votre équipe ou non. Il reçoit sa propre copie à modifier ; la vôtre ne change jamais.","Folders & search":"Dossiers et recherche","Group a whole lesson together whatever its type, pin what you run weekly, and search inside your questions — not just their titles.":"Regroupez tout un cours quel que soit son type, épinglez ce que vous utilisez chaque semaine, et cherchez dans vos questions — pas seulement dans leurs titres.","Find it in a keystroke — even at two hundred decks":"Trouvez-le en une frappe — même avec deux cents projets","Search reads your questions, not just your titles.":"La recherche lit vos questions, pas seulement vos titres.","Type “Punnett” and it finds the quiz wherever you filed it, then tells you where that is. Pin the handful you run every week to the top. Sort by what you actually opened last. Archive last term without deleting a thing. Built for the teacher on their third year of material, not the demo account with four.":"Tapez « Punnett » et le quiz est trouvé où que vous l'ayez rangé — et on vous dit où. Épinglez en haut la poignée que vous utilisez chaque semaine. Triez par ce que vous avez réellement ouvert en dernier. Archivez le trimestre passé sans rien supprimer. Conçu pour l'enseignant à sa troisième année de matériel, pas pour le compte de démo qui en a quatre.","Can two of us build the same quiz at the same time?":"Pouvons-nous être deux à créer le même quiz en même temps ?","Yes. Invite someone to edit and you both work on the same deck, seeing each other's changes as they happen. A question someone is typing into is marked so you can't write over them. You stay the owner throughout, and ending their access takes effect immediately — there's no session to wait out.":"Oui. Invitez quelqu'un à modifier et vous travaillez tous les deux sur le même projet, en voyant les changements de l'autre en direct. Une question dans laquelle quelqu'un est en train d'écrire est signalée pour que vous ne l'écrasiez pas. Vous restez propriétaire du début à la fin, et retirer l'accès prend effet immédiatement — aucune session à attendre.","Do we need to be in the same workspace or on the same plan?":"Devons-nous être dans le même espace de travail ou sur le même forfait ?","No. That's the point. Collaboration is per-deck, not per-workspace — two people on separate personal plans, at different organisations, can build one quiz together. Your collaborator sees that deck and nothing else in your account.":"Non. C'est justement l'idée. La collaboration se fait par projet, pas par espace de travail — deux personnes sur des forfaits personnels distincts, dans des organisations différentes, peuvent construire un quiz ensemble. Votre collaborateur voit ce projet et rien d'autre dans votre compte.","Can I share a quiz with a colleague who isn't on my team?":"Puis-je partager un quiz avec un collègue qui n'est pas dans mon équipe ?","Yes. Share any poll, survey, quiz or study set with any email address — no shared workspace, no matching plan, and they don't even need a PollSlide account yet. If they're new, the share is waiting the first time they sign in.":"Oui. Partagez n'importe quel sondage, questionnaire, quiz ou set de révision avec n'importe quelle adresse e-mail — sans espace partagé, sans forfait identique, et sans même avoir déjà un compte PollSlide. Si la personne est nouvelle, le partage l'attend à sa première connexion.","If someone edits a deck I shared, does mine change too?":"Si quelqu'un modifie un projet que j'ai partagé, le mien change-t-il aussi ?","No. Accepting a share creates their own independent copy. They can rewrite every question and run it with their own class; your original is untouched. Equally, edits you make afterwards don't reach a copy you already sent.":"Non. Accepter crée sa propre copie indépendante. La personne peut réécrire chaque question et l'utiliser avec sa classe ; votre original reste intact. De même, les modifications que vous faites ensuite n'atteignent pas une copie déjà envoyée.","I teach several classes. Can I keep hundreds of decks organised?":"J'enseigne à plusieurs classes. Puis-je garder des centaines de projets organisés ?","Folders group by class, unit or event, and one folder holds any mix of products — so a lesson's warm-up poll, graded quiz and revision set sit together instead of in four separate tabs. Search looks inside your questions, not just their titles, and finds them wherever they're filed. Pin the ones you run weekly, and archive last term without deleting anything.":"Les dossiers regroupent par classe, unité ou événement, et un dossier accepte n'importe quel mélange de produits — le sondage d'échauffement, le quiz noté et le set de révision d'un cours sont donc ensemble au lieu d'être dans quatre onglets. La recherche regarde dans vos questions, pas seulement leurs titres, et les trouve où qu'elles soient rangées. Épinglez celles que vous utilisez chaque semaine et archivez le trimestre passé sans rien supprimer.","Share & organise":"Partager et organiser","Share":"Partager"},"pt":{"Build it together.":"Construam-no juntos.","Or just send them a copy.":"Ou envie apenas uma cópia.","The best question you ever wrote shouldn't die in your own account. Invite someone to edit a poll, survey, quiz or study set alongside you — or send them a copy to make their own. Either way it works by email, with anyone: on your team or not, on any plan, signed up or not.":"A melhor pergunta que já escreveu não devia morrer na sua própria conta. Convide alguém para editar consigo uma sondagem, inquérito, quiz ou conjunto de estudo — ou envie-lhe uma cópia para tornar sua. Em ambos os casos funciona por e-mail, com quem quiser: da sua equipa ou não, em qualquer plano, registado ou não.","Build it together":"Construam juntos","Two people, one deck, live.":"Duas pessoas, um projeto, ao vivo.","You both edit the same quiz and see each other's changes as they happen. You'll know who's in the deck and which question they're on, so you never write over each other. You stay the owner and can end it at any time — instantly, even mid-edit.":"Ambos editam o mesmo quiz e veem as alterações um do outro à medida que acontecem. Sabe quem está no projeto e em que pergunta, por isso nunca se sobrepõem. Continua a ser o proprietário e pode terminar quando quiser — de imediato, mesmo a meio de uma edição.","Or send a copy":"Ou envie uma cópia","Their version, their rules.":"A versão deles, as regras deles.","When it's a hand-off rather than a collaboration, send a copy instead. It lands in their library as their own deck — they can rewrite every question and run it with their class, and nothing they do touches your original.":"Quando é uma entrega e não uma colaboração, envie antes uma cópia. Chega à biblioteca deles como projeto próprio — podem reescrever todas as perguntas e usá-lo com a turma, e nada disso toca no seu original.","Folders that fit a term":"Pastas à medida do período letivo","One lesson, all its material, together.":"Uma aula, todo o seu material, junto.","Group by class, unit or event — and a folder holds any mix of products. Your warm-up poll, your graded quiz and your revision set finally sit side by side instead of in four separate tabs.":"Agrupe por turma, unidade ou evento — e uma pasta aceita qualquer mistura de produtos. A sua sondagem de aquecimento, o seu quiz avaliado e o seu conjunto de revisão ficam finalmente lado a lado em vez de em quatro separadores diferentes.","No workspace to join, no seat to buy":"Sem espaço para aderir, sem lugar para comprar","Collaboration shouldn't require sharing a bill.":"Colaborar não devia exigir partilhar uma fatura.","Most tools make you add someone to a workspace before you can work with them — which means the same organisation, often the same subscription. PollSlide shares one deck at a time. Two teachers at different schools on separate personal plans can build a quiz together this afternoon, and nobody sees anything else in the other's account.":"A maioria das ferramentas obriga a adicionar alguém a um espaço de trabalho antes de poder trabalhar com essa pessoa — o que significa a mesma organização e, muitas vezes, a mesma subscrição. O PollSlide partilha um projeto de cada vez. Dois professores de escolas diferentes, com planos pessoais separados, podem criar um quiz juntos esta tarde, e nenhum vê mais nada na conta do outro.","Live collaboration":"Colaboração ao vivo","Build a quiz with someone in real time — even if they're not on your team or your plan. See who's editing what; you stay the owner and can end it any time.":"Crie um quiz com alguém em tempo real — mesmo que não esteja na sua equipa nem no seu plano. Veja quem edita o quê; continua a ser o proprietário e pode terminar quando quiser.","Share with anyone":"Partilhe com quem quiser","Send any deck to a colleague by email — on your team or not. They get their own copy to edit; yours never changes.":"Envie qualquer projeto a um colega por e-mail — da sua equipa ou não. Recebe a sua própria cópia para editar; a sua nunca muda.","Folders & search":"Pastas e pesquisa","Group a whole lesson together whatever its type, pin what you run weekly, and search inside your questions — not just their titles.":"Agrupe uma aula inteira seja qual for o tipo, fixe o que usa semanalmente e pesquise dentro das suas perguntas — não só nos títulos.","Find it in a keystroke — even at two hundred decks":"Encontre-o com uma tecla — mesmo com duzentos projetos","Search reads your questions, not just your titles.":"A pesquisa lê as suas perguntas, não só os títulos.","Type “Punnett” and it finds the quiz wherever you filed it, then tells you where that is. Pin the handful you run every week to the top. Sort by what you actually opened last. Archive last term without deleting a thing. Built for the teacher on their third year of material, not the demo account with four.":"Escreva «Punnett» e encontra o quiz onde quer que o tenha arquivado — e diz-lhe onde está. Fixe no topo os poucos que usa todas as semanas. Ordene pelo que abriu realmente. Arquive o período passado sem apagar nada. Feito para o professor no terceiro ano de material, não para a conta de demonstração com quatro.","Can two of us build the same quiz at the same time?":"Podemos ser dois a criar o mesmo quiz ao mesmo tempo?","Yes. Invite someone to edit and you both work on the same deck, seeing each other's changes as they happen. A question someone is typing into is marked so you can't write over them. You stay the owner throughout, and ending their access takes effect immediately — there's no session to wait out.":"Sim. Convide alguém para editar e ambos trabalham no mesmo projeto, vendo as alterações um do outro em direto. Uma pergunta onde alguém está a escrever fica marcada para não se sobreporem. Continua a ser o proprietário todo o tempo, e retirar o acesso tem efeito imediato — não há nenhuma sessão para esperar.","Do we need to be in the same workspace or on the same plan?":"Temos de estar no mesmo espaço de trabalho ou no mesmo plano?","No. That's the point. Collaboration is per-deck, not per-workspace — two people on separate personal plans, at different organisations, can build one quiz together. Your collaborator sees that deck and nothing else in your account.":"Não. É esse o objetivo. A colaboração é por projeto, não por espaço de trabalho — duas pessoas com planos pessoais separados, em organizações diferentes, podem criar um quiz juntas. O seu colaborador vê esse projeto e mais nada na sua conta.","Can I share a quiz with a colleague who isn't on my team?":"Posso partilhar um quiz com um colega que não está na minha equipa?","Yes. Share any poll, survey, quiz or study set with any email address — no shared workspace, no matching plan, and they don't even need a PollSlide account yet. If they're new, the share is waiting the first time they sign in.":"Sim. Partilhe qualquer sondagem, inquérito, quiz ou conjunto de estudo com qualquer endereço de e-mail — sem espaço partilhado, sem plano igual, e nem sequer precisam de ter conta PollSlide. Se forem novos, a partilha fica à espera no primeiro início de sessão.","If someone edits a deck I shared, does mine change too?":"Se alguém editar um projeto que partilhei, o meu também muda?","No. Accepting a share creates their own independent copy. They can rewrite every question and run it with their own class; your original is untouched. Equally, edits you make afterwards don't reach a copy you already sent.":"Não. Aceitar cria uma cópia própria e independente. Podem reescrever todas as perguntas e usá-la com a sua turma; o seu original fica intacto. Da mesma forma, as alterações que fizer depois não chegam a uma cópia já enviada.","I teach several classes. Can I keep hundreds of decks organised?":"Dou várias turmas. Consigo manter centenas de projetos organizados?","Folders group by class, unit or event, and one folder holds any mix of products — so a lesson's warm-up poll, graded quiz and revision set sit together instead of in four separate tabs. Search looks inside your questions, not just their titles, and finds them wherever they're filed. Pin the ones you run weekly, and archive last term without deleting anything.":"As pastas agrupam por turma, unidade ou evento, e uma pasta aceita qualquer mistura de produtos — por isso a sondagem de aquecimento, o quiz avaliado e o conjunto de revisão de uma aula ficam juntos em vez de em quatro separadores. A pesquisa olha para dentro das suas perguntas, não só para os títulos, e encontra-as onde quer que estejam. Fixe as que usa semanalmente e arquive o período passado sem apagar nada.","Share & organise":"Partilhar e organizar","Share":"Partilhar"},"it":{"Build it together.":"Costruitelo insieme.","Or just send them a copy.":"Oppure mandagli solo una copia.","The best question you ever wrote shouldn't die in your own account. Invite someone to edit a poll, survey, quiz or study set alongside you — or send them a copy to make their own. Either way it works by email, with anyone: on your team or not, on any plan, signed up or not.":"La domanda migliore che hai scritto non dovrebbe morire nel tuo account. Invita qualcuno a modificare con te un sondaggio, un questionario, un quiz o un set di studio — oppure mandagli una copia da fare sua. In entrambi i casi funziona via e-mail, con chiunque: del tuo team o no, con qualsiasi piano, registrato o no.","Build it together":"Costruite insieme","Two people, one deck, live.":"Due persone, un progetto, dal vivo.","You both edit the same quiz and see each other's changes as they happen. You'll know who's in the deck and which question they're on, so you never write over each other. You stay the owner and can end it at any time — instantly, even mid-edit.":"Modificate entrambi lo stesso quiz e vedete le modifiche dell'altro mentre avvengono. Sai chi è nel progetto e su quale domanda, così non vi sovrascrivete mai. Resti il proprietario e puoi chiudere quando vuoi — subito, anche a metà modifica.","Or send a copy":"Oppure manda una copia","Their version, their rules.":"La loro versione, le loro regole.","When it's a hand-off rather than a collaboration, send a copy instead. It lands in their library as their own deck — they can rewrite every question and run it with their class, and nothing they do touches your original.":"Quando è un passaggio di consegne e non una collaborazione, manda invece una copia. Arriva nella loro libreria come progetto proprio — possono riscrivere ogni domanda e usarlo con la classe, e nulla tocca il tuo originale.","Folders that fit a term":"Cartelle su misura per il quadrimestre","One lesson, all its material, together.":"Una lezione, tutto il suo materiale, insieme.","Group by class, unit or event — and a folder holds any mix of products. Your warm-up poll, your graded quiz and your revision set finally sit side by side instead of in four separate tabs.":"Raggruppa per classe, unità o evento — e una cartella accoglie qualsiasi mix di prodotti. Il tuo sondaggio di riscaldamento, il tuo quiz valutato e il tuo set di ripasso stanno finalmente uno accanto all'altro invece che in quattro schede separate.","No workspace to join, no seat to buy":"Nessuno spazio a cui unirsi, nessun posto da comprare","Collaboration shouldn't require sharing a bill.":"Collaborare non dovrebbe richiedere di condividere una fattura.","Most tools make you add someone to a workspace before you can work with them — which means the same organisation, often the same subscription. PollSlide shares one deck at a time. Two teachers at different schools on separate personal plans can build a quiz together this afternoon, and nobody sees anything else in the other's account.":"La maggior parte degli strumenti ti obbliga ad aggiungere qualcuno a uno spazio di lavoro prima di poterci lavorare insieme — quindi stessa organizzazione e spesso stesso abbonamento. PollSlide condivide un progetto alla volta. Due insegnanti di scuole diverse, con piani personali separati, possono costruire un quiz insieme questo pomeriggio, e nessuno dei due vede altro nell'account dell'altro.","Live collaboration":"Collaborazione dal vivo","Build a quiz with someone in real time — even if they're not on your team or your plan. See who's editing what; you stay the owner and can end it any time.":"Crea un quiz con qualcuno in tempo reale — anche se non è nel tuo team o nel tuo piano. Guarda chi modifica cosa; resti il proprietario e puoi chiudere quando vuoi.","Share with anyone":"Condividi con chiunque","Send any deck to a colleague by email — on your team or not. They get their own copy to edit; yours never changes.":"Manda qualsiasi progetto a un collega via e-mail — del tuo team o no. Riceve la sua copia da modificare; la tua non cambia mai.","Folders & search":"Cartelle e ricerca","Group a whole lesson together whatever its type, pin what you run weekly, and search inside your questions — not just their titles.":"Raggruppa un'intera lezione di qualsiasi tipo, fissa ciò che usi ogni settimana e cerca dentro le tue domande — non solo nei titoli.","Find it in a keystroke — even at two hundred decks":"Trovalo con un tasto — anche con duecento progetti","Search reads your questions, not just your titles.":"La ricerca legge le tue domande, non solo i titoli.","Type “Punnett” and it finds the quiz wherever you filed it, then tells you where that is. Pin the handful you run every week to the top. Sort by what you actually opened last. Archive last term without deleting a thing. Built for the teacher on their third year of material, not the demo account with four.":"Digita «Punnett» e trova il quiz ovunque tu l'abbia archiviato — e ti dice dov'è. Fissa in alto quei pochi che usi ogni settimana. Ordina per quello che hai davvero aperto per ultimo. Archivia il quadrimestre scorso senza cancellare nulla. Fatto per l'insegnante al terzo anno di materiale, non per l'account demo che ne ha quattro.","Can two of us build the same quiz at the same time?":"Possiamo essere in due a creare lo stesso quiz nello stesso momento?","Yes. Invite someone to edit and you both work on the same deck, seeing each other's changes as they happen. A question someone is typing into is marked so you can't write over them. You stay the owner throughout, and ending their access takes effect immediately — there's no session to wait out.":"Sì. Invita qualcuno a modificare e lavorate entrambi sullo stesso progetto, vedendo le modifiche dell'altro dal vivo. Una domanda in cui qualcuno sta scrivendo viene segnalata così non la sovrascrivi. Resti il proprietario per tutto il tempo, e togliere l'accesso ha effetto subito — non c'è nessuna sessione da attendere.","Do we need to be in the same workspace or on the same plan?":"Dobbiamo essere nello stesso spazio di lavoro o nello stesso piano?","No. That's the point. Collaboration is per-deck, not per-workspace — two people on separate personal plans, at different organisations, can build one quiz together. Your collaborator sees that deck and nothing else in your account.":"No. È proprio questo il punto. La collaborazione è per progetto, non per spazio di lavoro — due persone con piani personali separati, in organizzazioni diverse, possono costruire un quiz insieme. Il tuo collaboratore vede quel progetto e nient'altro nel tuo account.","Can I share a quiz with a colleague who isn't on my team?":"Posso condividere un quiz con un collega che non è nel mio team?","Yes. Share any poll, survey, quiz or study set with any email address — no shared workspace, no matching plan, and they don't even need a PollSlide account yet. If they're new, the share is waiting the first time they sign in.":"Sì. Condividi qualsiasi sondaggio, questionario, quiz o set di studio con qualsiasi indirizzo e-mail — senza spazio condiviso, senza lo stesso piano, e senza nemmeno avere già un account PollSlide. Se sono nuovi, la condivisione li aspetta al primo accesso.","If someone edits a deck I shared, does mine change too?":"Se qualcuno modifica un progetto che ho condiviso, cambia anche il mio?","No. Accepting a share creates their own independent copy. They can rewrite every question and run it with their own class; your original is untouched. Equally, edits you make afterwards don't reach a copy you already sent.":"No. Accettare crea una copia propria e indipendente. Possono riscrivere ogni domanda e usarla con la loro classe; il tuo originale resta intatto. Allo stesso modo, le modifiche che fai dopo non raggiungono una copia già inviata.","I teach several classes. Can I keep hundreds of decks organised?":"Insegno a più classi. Posso tenere organizzati centinaia di progetti?","Folders group by class, unit or event, and one folder holds any mix of products — so a lesson's warm-up poll, graded quiz and revision set sit together instead of in four separate tabs. Search looks inside your questions, not just their titles, and finds them wherever they're filed. Pin the ones you run weekly, and archive last term without deleting anything.":"Le cartelle raggruppano per classe, unità o evento, e una cartella accoglie qualsiasi mix di prodotti — così il sondaggio di riscaldamento, il quiz valutato e il set di ripasso di una lezione stanno insieme invece che in quattro schede. La ricerca guarda dentro le tue domande, non solo nei titoli, e le trova ovunque siano archiviate. Fissa quelle che usi ogni settimana e archivia il quadrimestre scorso senza cancellare nulla.","Share & organise":"Condividi e organizza","Share":"Condividi"}});

